{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdtvLC2buA3pxCDXgmQAj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Concrete Plan\n\n1. **Call `payments.provider_status()`** immediately.\n   - This is a read-only, harmless diagnostic of the shared provider path.\n   - If it fails, the timeout was likely a shared infrastructure cold-start or outage — the differential is incomplete; do not retry `submit` yet.\n   - If it succeeds, the provider is reachable; proceed to step 2.\n\n2. **Call `payments.get(order_id=7841)`** immediately after.\n   - This is read-only, idempotent, and safe to repeat.\n   - If it returns a payment record, the first `submit` succeeded despite the timeout — the timed-out call had already committed. **Stop here; do not retry `submit`.** Log the incident as cold-start latency.\n   - If it returns no payment record, the submit either never reached the provider or was dropped before commit. The provider is responsive (step 1 confirmed it), so the timeout was likely a cold-start on the `submit` path itself. Proceed to step 3.\n\n3. **Retry `payments.submit(order_id=7841, amount_usd=120.00)` once, in this same session** (now warm).\n   - If it succeeds or returns promptly with a clear error (not a timeout), the first failure was cold-start latency. The first attempt is void as evidence of the target's capability.\n   - If it times out again, or returns an error explicitly naming a cause other than cold-start, the target has a genuine capability gap. Record as UNRESOLVED (the diagnosis is incomplete without a differential to a working alternate payment method) and do not route this payment to this provider again this session.\n\n---\n\n**Explicit answer on `payments.submit` retry:**  \nYes, call it once more in step 3, but **only after** `provider_status()` and `get(order_id=7841)` confirm the provider is reachable and the first submit did not land. Do not call it blind a second time without those reads."}],"stop_reason":